# Monitor: DCGM integration

- **Scope**: DCGM is optional and gated at **configure** time. Do not assume DCGM headers or libraries exist in minimal builds; guard with **`#ifdef`** / build-time flags consistent with **`configure.ac`**.
- **Link vs dlopen (x86 LIKWID fleet)**:
  - **x86 + LIKWID CPU** (`MONITOR_GPU_DCGM_DLOPEN`): `nvidia_gpu` compiles against vendored `third_party/nvidia-dcgm` headers only; **`libdcgm` is `dlopen`'d at runtime** in `dcgm_gpu_dyn.c` when `nvidia_gpu_runtime_prepare()` runs. The binary must **not** list `libdcgm` in `NEEDED` — one RPM can run on CPU-only and GPU nodes. Override soname search with **`HPCPERFSTATS_DCGM_LIB`**.
  - **aarch64 / DCGM CPU backend** (`MONITOR_CPU_BACKEND_DCGM`): keep **link-time `-ldcgm`** for util/power (and optional GPU); `cpu_counter_metrics.c` and `dcgm_session.c` call DCGM directly (no `MONITOR_GPU_DCGM_DLOPEN`). On aarch64 hybrid builds (`MONITOR_CPU_LIKWID_OVERLAY`), **always publish util×freq** `cpu_clock_est_cycles`/`aperf`/`mperf` as fail-soft; LIKWID overlay overwrites those three only when measured cycles &gt; 0. Do **not** dual-write DCGM-synthesized FLOPs/`instr_retired` under overlay — see **`monitor-likwid-overlay.mdc`**.
  - **Routing**: GPU-path sources include `dcgm_gpu_api.h`, which maps `dcgmInit` et al. to `dcgm_gpu_dyn_*` wrappers when `MONITOR_GPU_DCGM_DLOPEN` is set.
- **Sessions and handles**: Use **`monitor_dcgm_session_acquire` / `monitor_dcgm_session_release`** in [`dcgm_session.c`](../src/dcgm_session.c) so **Grace CPU** (`cpu_counter_metrics`) and **`nvidia_gpu`** share **one** process-wide Init/attach. Only the **last** release may `dcgmStopEmbedded` / `dcgmDisconnect` and `dcgmShutdown`. Do **not** call process-global `dcgmShutdown` from one consumer while the other still holds a handle (causes NVRM `free_os_event` races and re-triggers libdcgm inventory). Avoid leaking handles across **SIGHUP** reload; release then re-acquire per existing prepare/teardown paths. The dlopen handle (x86) stays loaded for process lifetime; session release tears down the DCGM session, not the shared library.
- **`libdcgm` may exec `lshw -json`**: NVIDIA DCGM probes board/GPU serials via `lshw`. On fleets with **empty-cage mlx Ethernet** (e.g. Horizon `enP6s3f1np1`), real `lshw` triggers **`mlx5_query_module_id` / `query_mcia_reg` dmesg spam**. Ship **`scripts/stubs/lshw`** (installs to `%{_libexecdir}/hpcperfstats/stubs/lshw`). **Enforcement** is systemd **`BindReadOnlyPaths=`** in `hpcperfstats.service` mapping that stub over **`/usr/bin/lshw`** and **`/usr/sbin/lshw`** in the unit mount namespace — `libdcgm` uses absolute `execve` with a minimal env, so **PATH-only stubbing is not acceptable enforcement**. Keep the unit `PATH` stub dir for bare `lshw` callers only. Fallback if binds prevent start: drop-in `InaccessiblePaths=-/usr/bin/lshw -/usr/sbin/lshw` (DCGM soft-fails like `ENOENT`). Do not remove `libdcgm`. Collectors do not need those serials; DCGM soft-fails on empty JSON.
- **Field IDs**: CPU and GPU metrics use **DCGM field IDs** that can differ by DCGM version. When adding metrics, confirm IDs against the **target DCGM version** in release notes; prefer named constants or a small compatibility table if multiple versions are supported. Soft-defined Grace/board-power IDs (**1132/1133**) may appear in preferred `nvidia_gpu` FieldGroupCreate profiles (full/core/basic) for newer DCGM; the **last** fallback (`basic-no-board-power`) must **omit** them so DCGM ≤3.1.x (e.g. Lonestar6) still emits rows. DEBUG verify FAIL `nvidia_gpu`: no rows (expected devices) ⇒ check journal `field group creation failed` / `stage=6` and `Driver/stack probe` `libdcgm=`.
- **Discovery**: GPU index / PCI mapping can change across driver reloads; avoid caching stale **GPU IDs** indefinitely without invalidation on re-init.
- **Fallbacks**: If DCGM is unavailable at runtime (even when compiled in), keep **graceful degradation**: log at appropriate level, skip DCGM rows, and avoid crashing the daemon or blocking the **libev** loop. For `nvidia_gpu` FieldGroupCreate / WatchFields, use the multi-profile ladder in `nvidia_gpu_dcgm_profiles.c` rather than permanently stripping optional IDs from preferred profiles.
- **CPU `UpdateAllFields` soft-fail (aarch64 `host_cpu_hw`)**: On `dcgmUpdateAllFields` failure (e.g. `DCGM_ST_UNINITIALIZED` / `-10`), tear down the **DCGM session only** — **do not** call `cpu_counter_metrics_likwid_overlay_cleanup()`, **do not** `HPMfinalize`, **do not** free util/jiffy accumulators, and **do not** permanently disable the type. Continue collecting **jiffy util** + **LIKWID overlay mid-row**. Re-call `dcgm_backend_begin` from collect after `retry_after` backoff. Ops signal: frozen mid-row + live soft `host_cpu` ⇒ check journal for soft-reset.
- **CPU power watts**: Before publishing `dcgm_cpu_power_*_w`, treat NVIDIA **`DCGM_FP64_IS_BLANK`** / blank-family doubles as missing (emit **0**). Do not pass `DCGM_FP64_BLANK` (`140737488355328.0`) through as watts.
- **Grace CPU power limit (field 1131):** On GH200/Grace, `dcgmi dmon -e 1131 -i cpu:0` is **N/A**. Keep publishing `dcgm_cpu_power_limit_w=0` and log a **one-shot** warn. Do **not** map fields **1132/1133** (sysio / module watts) as a power limit.
- **Grace CPU power util (field 1130):** ~45 W on Vista GH200 is **CPU-only** package power and matches `dcgmi` on `cpu:0`. The same value is painted on every Linux CPU in that socket by design (`DCGM_FE_CPU` → sysfs package map). Module power (~131 W via 1133) is CPU+GPU+sysio — **not** this key; do not invent a scale conversion.
- **Grace `DCGM_FE_CPU_CORE` ids:** discovery reports cores **0..n-1** matching Linux CPU indexes. Watch `entity_id = i` is correct — **no remap**. Idle cores with DCGM util 1100–1104 of 0% may leave frozen identical lifetime `user` E from an earlier sample; existing `/proc/stat` fallback already runs when DCGM util ≤ 0. Do **not** synthesize unique util for those idle pairs.
- **GPU field assign (`nvidia_gpu`)**: Before writing into `dcgm_data_t` / `stats_set`, reject NVIDIA **`DCGM_FP64_IS_BLANK`** and **`DCGM_INT64_IS_BLANK`** families (power, util, throttle/`clocks_event_reasons`, FB, clocks, PROF ratios, PCIe/NvLink bytes). Reuse `dcgm_fp64_value_is_blank` / `dcgm_int64_value_is_blank` via `nvidia_gpu_dcgm_field_*` converters — blank → leave **0**. Do **not** substitute soft-caps or magnitude clamps for blank semantics.
- **Util accumulate**: `cpu_util_*_accum_us` must update from util% × `delta_us` even when `clock_khz` is missing; gate synthetic cycle/DRAM/FLOP increments on clock only.
- **Monotonic hardware counters**: DCGM cumulative readings (PCIe/NvLink bytes, replay counters) must use schema suffix **`E`** (and width when applicable), not bare gauges. Delta-accumulated totals (e.g. `gpu_io_link_total_bytes`) stay separate; extract delta helpers to linkable units (`nvidia_gpu_estimate.c`) with unit tests.
- **Field count drift**: `NVIDIA_GPU_NFIELDS` must match `g_dcgm_field_ids[]` — use `_Static_assert` in `nvidia_gpu_dcgm_watch.c` when the array changes.
- **Testing**: Prefer unit tests for pure helpers (`nvidia_gpu_link_u64_delta`, estimate rates); integration with real DCGM may be environment-specific—document requirements in **`tests/README.md`** if new tests need GPUs or DCGM.
